{"availability":"available","full":"pseudobarbie8/hf-rag-demo","name":"hf-rag-demo","description":"A minimal retrieval-augmented generation demo built with Sentence Transformers + Streamlit. Live on Hugging Face.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-31T10:55:00Z","updated":"2026-09-03T11:02:24Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/pseudobarbie/rag-demo","topics":["demo","huggingface","rag"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/pseudobarbie/rag-demo","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:02:06.903Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:02:06.903Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:02:06.903Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T11:09:21.577Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T21:02:06.903Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Minimal retrieval-augmented generation demo for legal contract clauses. Built with Sentence Transformers + Streamlit.","Generic embeddings fail on contract language in a specific, measurable way. \"Either party may terminate for convenience\" and \"Neither party may terminate for convenience\" are near-identical in vector space and opposite in law. A retriever tuned on web text returns both in the top-3 and the generator picks one. The answer is fluent, confident, and wrong.","This model is fine-tuned against exactly that failure: hard negatives are mined from clause pairs that are lexically near-identical and semantically opposite."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pseudobarbie8/hf-rag-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"656653b4612db2f93ce067c9a227acf579eded10f47273e7cc5245377f80d7bf","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:21.785Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:21.785Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Minimal retrieval-augmented generation demo for legal contract clauses. Built with Sentence Transformers + Streamlit.","sourceUrl":"https://